.Dd December 6, 2025
.Dt bastille-template 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bastille template
.Nd Apply templates to jail(s).
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm bastille template
.Op Fl a
.Ar TARGET TEMPLATE
.Op Fl -arg Ar KEY=VALUE
.Op Fl -arg-file Ar FILE
.Nm bastille template
.Sy convert Ar TEMPLATE
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm bastille template
sub-command will apply the specified
.Ar TEMPLATE
to
.Ar TARGET .
Additionally, it can convert a
.Ar TEMPLATE
to the new Bastillefile syntax.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy bastille template Oo Fl a Oc Ar TARGET TEMPLATE Oo Fl -arg Ar KEY=VALUE Oc Oo Fl -arg-file Ar FILE Oc
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a , Fl -auto
Auto mode. Start/stop jail(s) if required.
.It Fl -arg Ar KEY=VALUE
Specify any number of args to pass to the template.
These arg names should already be present in the template, or
they will not apply. Args passed via the command line will
override the included template args.
.It Fl -arg-file Ar FILE
Specify a file containing arg replacements to be passed to
the template. The arg names should already be present in
the template. These args will override the included template
args.
.El
.It Sy bastille template convert Ar TEMPLATE
.Pp
This will convert an older style template to the new Bastillefile
syntax. Older styles used one file per hook, named after the hook.
Bastillefile templates include all hooks inside the Bastillefile.
.Pp
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Apply www/nginx to myjail:
.Sy bastille template myjail www/nginx
